ed":12,"play_caller":"Liam Coen"},{"season":2022,"team":"CLE","distance":0.7325,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kevin Stefanski"},{"season":2024,"team":"LV","distance":0.7451,"shared":12,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2025,"team":"NO","distance":0.2563,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Brandon Staley"},{"season":2024,"team":"CHI","distance":0.3215,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"WAS","distance":0.3273,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"CAR","distance":0.4141,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Ejiro Evero"},{"season":2023,"team":"SF","distance":0.4494,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Cardinals are 2-4 through week 6 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 178 to 126. The offense has been carrying the team, ranking 17th in EPA per play while the defense sits 28th in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the lowest play-action rate and the 3rd lowest eight man box rate in the league.","offense":"The Cardinals offense has been about average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Schematically, they stand out for the lowest play-action rate and an RPO rate that was among the lowest in the league. Jacoby Brissett has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Trey McBride, who has drawn 29% of the targets.","defense":"The Cardinals have one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 25th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area has been EPA allowed per rush, where it ranks 8th, and its weakest has been EPA allowed per dropback, where it ranks 30th. Josh Sweat has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Budda Baker, who has 3.5 sacks, after doing little as a pass rusher a year ago. In terms of scheme, they have the 3rd lowest eight man box rate in the league.","special":"The Cardinals have been one of the most conservative teams on fourth down, going for it on only 0% of their short-yardage chances. Their kickers have made 88% of field goals, which is about average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into tight ends, about 10% of the money on the books.","players":"Jacoby Brissett has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,328 yards. Trey McBride has been the clear top target with 29% of the looks and 361 receiving yards. The backfield has been a committee led by Jeremiyah Love and Tyler Allgeier. On defense, Budda Baker leads the team with 3.5 sacks.","coaching":"Mike LaFleur is calling the offense as head coach and Nick Rallis is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 Jets under Mike LaFleur and the 2022 Steelers. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Saints under Brandon Staley and the 2024 Bears.","trends":"The offense went from 23rd in EPA per play in 2025 to 17th so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 27th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 28th so far this season, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was play-action rate, which went from 25% to 16%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}